§ `fixtures`

`WIRC` MEANS `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013`
`ACA`  MEANS `the Accident Compensation Act 1985`

`15 August 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 8 2026
`15 August 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 8 2025
`30 June 2025`   MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2025
`1 July 2025`    MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2025
`30 June 2026`   MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2026
`1 July 2026`    MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2026
`30 June 2027`   MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2027
`1 July 2027`    MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2027
`1 March 2025`   MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2025

`a claim on 1 March 2018`     MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2018
`a claim on 1 June 1995`      MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 1995
`a claim on 11 November 1997` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 11 1997
`a claim on 12 November 1997` MEANS `the calendar date` 12 11 1997
`a claim on 4 April 2010`     MEANS `the calendar date` 4 4 2010
`a claim on 5 April 2010`     MEANS `the calendar date` 5 4 2010

-- The not-covered answers, for an answer of any type.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`day gap` MEANS `not covered` `the day is outside 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027, the two years the notice's columns cover`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`no row` MEANS `not covered` `the notice prints no row for this under the Act named`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`no maximum weekly payment` MEANS `not covered` `the notice prints no maximum weekly payment for this entitlement period, work capacity and claim`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`no band` MEANS `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for an impairment rating in this band under the Act named`

GIVEN a IS AN `Answer` `Impairment figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`printed amounts in` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `answered` f THEN JUST (f's `amounts`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS AN `Answer` `Impairment figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`provision in` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `answered` f THEN JUST (f's `provision`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN NOTHING

§ `the period rule`

-- The "before" column runs 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026; the "from" column 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027 (lines 28-29,
-- 408-409). s 161(a)(ii), line 498: $2,930 before, $3,000 from.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `30 June 2025` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `day gap`
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `1 July 2025` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 2930
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `30 June 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 2930
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `1 July 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 3000
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `30 June 2027` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 3000
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `1 July 2027` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `day gap`
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `ACA` `1 March 2025` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `day gap`
#ASSERT `the deemed pre-injury earnings the notice sets for me` `WIRC` `1 July 2027` `Schedule item 1, column 3, paragraph (c): where no rate is applicable` EQUALS `day gap`
#ASSERT `the amounts the notice prints for my rating` `WIRC` `30 June 2025` `a permanent impairment` `a whole person impairment` 15 EQUALS `day gap`

§ `weekly payments, 2013 Act (lines 495-530)`

-- s 161(b)(ii): $3,000 less current weekly earnings: 3000 - 500 = 2500.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 EQUALS `answered` 2500
-- Before column: 2930 - 500 = 2430.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2025` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 EQUALS `answered` 2430
-- Earnings above the maximum: 3000 - 3500 is below nothing, read as 0.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 3500 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- s 162(a)(ii): $3,000.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the second entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 3000
-- s 162(b)(ii): 3000 - 80% of 1000 = 3000 - 800 = 2200; before: 2930 - 800 = 2130.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the second entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 EQUALS `answered` 2200
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2025` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the second entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 EQUALS `answered` 2130
-- s 163(2)(b), printed under "no current work capacity" yet less 80%: 3000 - 0.8 x 250 = 3000 - 200 = 2800.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `after the second entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 250 EQUALS `answered` 2800
-- s 165(5)(b): approved, 3000 - 0.8 x 1500 = 3000 - 1200 = 1800.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `after the second entitlement period` TRUE FALSE TRUE 1500 EQUALS `answered` 1800
-- A current work capacity after the second entitlement period, no approved application: no row.
#ASSERT `the most I can be paid each week` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `after the second entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1500 EQUALS `no maximum weekly payment`

-- After the maximum: the formula amount or the ceiling, whichever is less.
-- First period, no capacity: formula 3200 > 3000, so 3000; formula 2400 < 3000, so 2400.
#ASSERT `my weekly payments after the maximum` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 3200 EQUALS `answered` 3000
#ASSERT `my weekly payments after the maximum` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 2400 EQUALS `answered` 2400
-- Second period, capacity, earnings 1000: ceiling 2200; formula 1600 -> 1600; formula 2500 -> 2200.
#ASSERT `my weekly payments after the maximum` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the second entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 1600 EQUALS `answered` 1600
#ASSERT `my weekly payments after the maximum` `WIRC` `15 August 2026` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the second entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 2500 EQUALS `answered` 2200
#ASSERT `my weekly payments after the maximum` `WIRC` `1 July 2027` `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the second entitlement period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 2500 EQUALS `day gap`
-- Finding 4: a worker whose weekly payments were last indexed on 1 September 2025 (anniversary) is still on the "before"
-- figures on a day in August 2026: 2930.
#ASSERT `my weekly payments after the maximum` `WIRC` (`the calendar date` 1 9 2025) `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 3200 EQUALS `answered` 2930
-- Finding 4, a worker not yet indexed: entitlement to weekly payments began on 1 March 2026, asked about August 2026, before
-- the first anniversary. The input is the day the entitlement began, 1 March 2026, in the "before" column (1 July 2025 to
-- 30 June 2026): s 161(a)(ii), line 498, $2,930; formula 3200 -> 2930.
#ASSERT `my weekly payments after the maximum` `WIRC` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `a claim on 1 March 2018` `the first entitlement period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 3200 EQUALS `answered` 2930

